	"threatinc_marineVeterancyEffectMax": 1.0,
	"threatinc_marineVeterancyLossReduction": 0.5,
	# a hard fight teaches, a curbstomp teaches nothing: xp is
	# (1 - effectiveness) x headcount x this, vanilla's own raid figure
	"threatinc_marineXpPerBattle": 0.2,
	# what an NPC or Threat landing musters at (0 raw, 1 elite)
	"threatinc_npcLandingVeterancy": 0.15,
	# landings inherit the player fleet's marine rank and write back what they
	# earned on withdrawal, and the ground skills apply to the player's fronts
	"threatinc_marineFleetXpTransfer": true,
	# a tactical pass with a front deployed costs it this fraction of its
	# marines - and in exchange the strike's disruption also lands on the
	# Fabrication Core and port (the ground forces mark targets)
	"threatinc_frontDangerCloseEnabled": true,
	# per bombardment day (a bombardment is one day since 2026-09-28)
	"threatinc_frontDangerCloseLossFraction": 0.005,
	# Threat doctrine over its own besieged world (2026-09-06): while Defense
	# Swarms or any armed Threat fleet hold the orbit over an enemy front with
	# no armed hostile fleet there to contest them, a countdown runs; at
	# threatScourDays the hive saturation-bombards its own surface - the front
	# is annihilated to the last marine and fallout closes the ground. A fleet
	# over the planet (Escort, Guard, the player) stops the clock; leaving it
	# resets nothing but its own presence. The board's Attack cell shows
	# "scour N d" while it runs.
	# Minimum total Threat fleet points in orbit (garrison Defense Swarms and any
	# Threat combat fleet within 1,500u) for the swarm to "hold the orbit" for a
	# scour: a saturation bombardment is a fleet operation, not something a lone
	# battered frigate can mount. Below this the swarm holds nothing - the clock
	# resets (a remnant is not a bombardment platform). The smallest real Defense
	# Swarm is ~83 FP and a stray frigate ~5-15, so 50 separates them; raise it
	# toward 150-300 to demand a serious battle group.
	# the swarm grinds an enemy front it has the orbit over, rather than
	# annihilating it on a timer (the scour, removed 2026-09-08): this
	# fraction of the front per 30 days, scaled by its weight over the planet
	"threatinc_swarmFrontBombardPer30Days": 0.60,
	# the swarm's bombardment in proportion to the fleet points over the planet (user, 2026-10-12: "shouldn't
	# be proportional to the FP overhead?" - the fraction rule above capped it at 2% of the front a day whatever
	# the weight): marines killed a day per fleet point, divided by the front's cover (dug in up to 1.5x) and
	# scaled by its veterancy; 0 falls back to the fraction rule
	"threatinc_swarmBombardMarinesPerFPDay": 0.05,
	# fuel a day of that bombardment draws from the swarm's stock per fleet point (2.86 is the human saturation
	# rate, satFuelPerFPDay); a day the stock cannot pay is skipped and logged; 0 free
	"threatinc_swarmBombardFuelPerFPDay": 2.86,
	# a swarm fleet carries its ordnance (user, 2026-10-12, after the central stock paid 61k fuel over 18 days
	# for a hive whose port was offline: "the swarm pays nothing for fuel and they could keep bombarding"):
	# this many days of swarmBombardFuelPerFPDay, drawn from the stock at first use (the launch load) and
	# refilled only at a hive whose port stands undisrupted with its imports not fully cut; dry over a hive
	# that cannot arm it, a garrison swarm flies to the nearest hive that can and comes back
	"threatinc_swarmBombardHoldDays": 10,
	# the stock arms a hold only above its reserve: this many months of the hive's fuel income, on top of the
	# founding kit (the user, 2026-10-13, after hw165-hw171: five of 21 games fell to the bombardment draining the
	# stock to 0 - "only take fuel for bombard in the first place if reserves are good"); 0 arms from any stock
	"threatinc_swarmBombardReserveMonths": 1,
	# under the reserve a dry swarm over its own besieged hive breaks up its ships into the hive's ground troops
	# (fabricateTroopsPerFP a point, smallest first, flagship and last hull spared) instead of bombarding - "they
	# can go with no fuel and just reinforce the front right by breaking up ships"; a fuel-rich navy never does
	"threatinc_hiveBreakUpEnabled": true,
	# a relief force holding the orbit over its own invaded world bombards the Threat army on the same formula while
	# the defenders are losing (the army pushes, or holds and the next counter-attack would not overrun it), paying
	# fuel from what it carries above its passage home and then its supply line (2026-10-03, the user); 0 off
	"threatinc_reliefBombardPer30Days": 0.60,
	# relief holds the orbit until the Threat army is gone, or until it is worn below defendMinStrength and the swarm
